# Swift & SwiftUI conventions

The project defaults to `SWIFT_DEFAULT_ACTOR_ISOLATION = MainActor` under Swift
6 language mode, so anything crossing an actor boundary must say so explicitly.

- SwiftUI only for UI. Prefer `@Observable` over `ObservableObject`.
- Prefer `async`/`await` over completion handlers. A `Task` started by a view
  must be cancelled when the view disappears.
- Value types that cross the actor boundary need `nonisolated` — including
  their `Equatable` conformance, or Swift 6 rejects even an `==` comparison.
- New unit tests use Swift Testing (`@Test`, `#expect`, `#require`), matching
  `RoomLensTests`. UI tests stay on XCTest.
- No third-party dependencies without asking first.

```swift
// ❌ BAD — main-actor isolated by default, so this cannot cross to the actor.
struct CaptureState: Equatable { ... }

// ✅ GOOD
nonisolated struct CaptureState: Equatable { ... }
```

Formatting is `xcrun swift-format` and runs automatically after edits; a commit
is blocked if staged Swift fails `swift-format lint --strict`.
